      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hereditary angioneurotic edema is a dominant autosomal disease (incidence 1/150,000), whose diagnosis is crucial as this condition can lead to fatal asphyxia within minutes. We report the case of a three-year-old girl, misdiagnosed as allergic asthma. Recognition of the syndrome led to adapted care restoring normal family and school life. Pathogenic cascades involved and therapeutic principles of this disease are reviewed."},
